WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.090
Hello, I'm Gav.
I'm Dan.

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:03.740
We're the Slow Mo Guys.

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:04.820
It's June, isn't it.

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:06.620
Know what that means?
I do.

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:08.040
Giant balloons.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.500
Although this ones all skanky.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.400
That is about a year old I think.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.750
Been in the shed since last June.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:15.660
We've only got enough for
just one video this June.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:16.860
We're not gonna do a full month.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:18.290
But I was recently watching

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:19.910
the original giant balloon video

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.360
which has over 170 million views

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:23.240
at the time of recording.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.070
And there was a GoPro looking down

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:27.260
and I thought, landing on a balloon

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.630
and seeing it from above
would look very cool.

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:30.463
Well, you're right,

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:32.480
but now it meas that your
gonna have to film the slow mo

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:33.730
and I'm gonna be the one jumping.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:36.020
I've had enough of jumping
from heights recently.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:36.853
Yeah?

00:00:36.853 --> 00:00:37.990
Just finished breaking my wrist.

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:41.190
Jumping onto some wood.

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:42.288
Just got done with that?
Yeah.

00:00:42.288 --> 00:00:43.500
I'm finished with that.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.100
So you'll be up the ladder.
Yep.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.760
Hopefully only breaking the
balloon, not your wrist.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:49.230
And I'll be on the roof,

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:52.316
hopefully not breaking
the camera or my legs.

00:00:52.316 --> 00:00:53.670
That's the plan.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:55.116
That's a tall order, this one.

00:00:55.116 --> 00:00:56.410
I really hope I don't break anything.

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:57.243
Yeah, me too.

00:00:57.243 --> 00:00:58.076
Here we are again.

00:00:58.076 --> 00:00:59.470
I'm actually kind of looking forward to

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:00.330
being splashed to this,

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:01.163
it's really warm.

00:01:01.163 --> 00:01:02.192
It's bloody hot, innit?

00:01:02.192 --> 00:01:03.025
Yeah.

00:01:03.025 --> 00:01:03.858
So this is our standard procedure,

00:01:03.858 --> 00:01:04.700
red six-footer.

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:08.040
I didn't think that in 2010
we'd be doing these in 2018.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:08.873
Neither did I.

00:01:08.873 --> 00:01:09.706
You think you would've been

00:01:09.706 --> 00:01:11.419
doing something different with your life?

00:01:11.419 --> 00:01:13.630
Yes, actually.

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:14.870
Hopefully this cushions you enough

00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:16.560
to not hit the ground beneath.

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:17.393
Yeah.

00:01:18.434 --> 00:01:19.267
Hopefully.

00:01:19.267 --> 00:01:20.270
You want me to swan dive?

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:21.830
I feel like if you swan dive,

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:24.260
that's spreading your weight more evenly.

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:25.240
Than what?

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:27.183
Than like, hitting your legs on it.

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:30.000
Yeah, but your legs are
supposed to go first.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.030
You don't ever let like...

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:32.236
Not on to something softer.

00:01:32.236 --> 00:01:33.577
You don't go to gymnastics and go,

00:01:33.577 --> 00:01:35.906
"Mate, you land chin first," and then...

00:01:37.207 --> 00:01:39.744
"And finish the vault with
a swan dive onto the floor."

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:41.703
But think about it,

00:01:41.703 --> 00:01:43.230
if you're landing on
something soft and uneven,

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:45.340
don't really wanna land on your ankles,

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:46.580
I would say.

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:48.120
So we've sort of learnt that,

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:49.000
when you fill one of these,

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.210
the weight of the water sort of crushes

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:53.780
a lot of the slack underneath,

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.520
leaving the top to become very tight.

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:59.370
So we thought it was a good
idea to massage the balloon.

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:01.350
And you can actually feel and hear it,

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:02.963
like, creaking when you do it.

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:06.603
You can hear that slightly.

00:02:06.603 --> 00:02:08.758
Yes, you're just adding
some of it's slack.

00:02:08.758 --> 00:02:09.591
You're just adding some slack

00:02:09.591 --> 00:02:11.960
to the the top rather
than the bottom by...

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:16.281
It's like weird 'cause
the side move around like

00:02:16.281 --> 00:02:17.114
Yeah.

00:02:17.114 --> 00:02:17.947
Every time I do it.

00:02:17.947 --> 00:02:19.660
I'm nervous, this is my nervous face.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:23.030
Looks pretty nervous.

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:24.610
When you're up there,

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:26.570
'cause I'm six foot tall,

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:28.670
if I'm on an eight foot ladder,

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:31.020
it makes it really high.

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:33.270
I don't think this is a six foot balloon.

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:34.290
It's certainly looks like

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:36.210
it's filling up like at the neck,

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:38.650
which means its almost full to capacity.

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:41.130
It looks extra bloated,

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:42.470
but it's not very .

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:45.090
I swear the one I jumped on spread wider.

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:47.719
Maybe it's 'cause its been
in the shed since June.

00:02:47.719 --> 00:02:48.960
Maybe we've gotta get better balloons.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:49.793
Yeah.

00:02:53.168 --> 00:02:54.001
What?

00:02:54.001 --> 00:02:55.183
Let's give it a shove.

00:02:57.270 --> 00:02:58.850
Out we go.

00:02:58.850 --> 00:02:59.683
You'll pass it to me, yeah.

00:02:59.683 --> 00:03:00.516
Yeah.

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:05.280
Not a good start.

00:03:07.369 --> 00:03:09.290
Now if you fall, grab on to the gutter.

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:11.060
It'll definitely break,

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:12.610
which should slow you down just enough.

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:13.681
Great.

00:03:13.681 --> 00:03:15.010
'Scuse me.

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:15.940
Okay, I'm good.

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:17.040
I'll head back down.

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:20.590
What did you do today?

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:22.300
Oh, you know.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:23.510
Just climbed out on my roof

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:27.250
and dangled a high-speed cinema camera

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:31.080
while some other bloke
jumped on a balloon.

00:03:32.056 --> 00:03:33.160
You all right?

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:33.993
Yeah.

00:03:37.608 --> 00:03:39.160
You ready to take now, should I go?

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:39.993
All right.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:49.720
How was that?

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:50.920
Oh, I got winded.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:52.967
You all right?

00:03:52.967 --> 00:03:55.050
Actually, yeah.

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:57.580
I went for it, winded
myself when I landed.

00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:00.800
'Cause it was kind of like,
belly flopping but not.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:03.130
'Cause you belly flop and you just go...

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:04.020
And then it burst.

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:05.560
It felt like I landed, went...

00:04:06.804 --> 00:04:08.190
So it was kind of like landing

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:11.444
on a fat cushion of water.

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:26.950
Oh, the ripples.

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:27.783
Wow.

00:04:27.783 --> 00:04:29.070
The half of that balloon's burst

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:30.507
by the time of the other
half even realizes it.

00:04:30.507 --> 00:04:32.070
It's like it forgets.

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:32.903
And then I think,

00:04:32.903 --> 00:04:34.000
the pressure that you forced

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.720
into the side that hasn't burst

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:37.426
then splits right down the middle.

00:04:37.426 --> 00:04:39.096
Oh.

00:04:39.096 --> 00:04:41.640
Look at your face, Daniel.

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.480
I was winded by that.

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:46.460
I like the spread of the water.

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:47.293
It's perfectly even,

00:04:47.293 --> 00:04:48.270
you haven't got a shot of that before

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:50.360
where it's completely from above.

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:52.710
You can totally see the spread there.

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:54.860
There's you moving.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:56.810
Here's me pressing the trigger

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:58.176
and trying not to fall off the roof.

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:00.543
So a lot of the time

00:05:00.543 --> 00:05:02.170
whenever we just have one Phantom going,

00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:04.420
I like to get it a couple of times

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:06.220
from multiple focal lengths.

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:07.920
I like to get the wide first, you know.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:08.753
Make sure we've got it.

00:05:08.753 --> 00:05:10.200
Then go in for a nice close up.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.300
And if I botched the focus,
you know, it's not a big deal

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:13.470
because we've already got the wide.

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:14.770
I like it.

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:16.070
So that means we have to do it again?

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:16.903
Yep!

00:05:16.903 --> 00:05:18.569
I'm actually okay with it.

00:05:18.569 --> 00:05:20.540
Because it is really hot out here,

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:21.840
and I am nice and refreshed.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.640
You're probably sweating
up there on the roof.

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:24.473
I'll tell you what.

00:05:24.473 --> 00:05:25.306
Having a miserable time.

00:05:25.306 --> 00:05:26.733
It's very hot on the knees.

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:28.426
I was like straddling it.

00:05:28.426 --> 00:05:29.700
My knees were burning up there.

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:33.993
I should've got some sort of
handheld accessories for this.

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:43.310
Oh, oh gosh.

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:45.997
You all right?

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:50.107
You okay?

00:05:50.107 --> 00:05:50.940
Just about.

00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:53.610
That one wasn't as good as the one.

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:55.150
It like burst as I hit it,

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:57.730
so I just pretty much
hit the floor that time.

00:05:57.730 --> 00:05:58.563
Oh man.

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:01.348
You slid quite a long way.

00:06:01.348 --> 00:06:03.750
Yeah I did, I...

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:04.920
I was very surprised at this one,

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:06.130
'cause I was filming like this.

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:07.910
But you slid so far.

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:09.010
So I actually had to track you

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:10.720
because it was a tighter shot.

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:11.700
That's a hell of a move.

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:14.492
Being on the roof, being
like, improvising, track that.

00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:17.113
Top of your head.

00:06:17.113 --> 00:06:18.500
Lovely bald spot going on there.

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:20.090
Friar tuck action.

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:22.660
Almost identical way of falling as well.

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:25.440
Yeah, I think you've
definitely found your way.

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:26.690
And then it split.

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:27.840
It split from around the edge

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:28.673
and came up to me.

00:06:28.673 --> 00:06:29.932
That's a weird one, innit.

00:06:29.932 --> 00:06:31.400
I don't think we've seen that before.

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:34.170
You see on this one, I pretty
much just hit the floor

00:06:34.170 --> 00:06:35.630
and the balloon sort of got in the way.

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:38.880
On the first one, it felt
like almost like cushioned me

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:40.850
and then let me go, it
was much more comfortable.

00:06:40.850 --> 00:06:43.280
This one was just sort of like, bang.

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:44.190
If I speed this one up,

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:45.663
you can see how far you slid.

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:48.845
Good tracking job there!

00:06:48.845 --> 00:06:49.678
Oh, cheers, thanks.

00:06:49.678 --> 00:06:50.511
Solid.

00:06:50.511 --> 00:06:52.010
As with any sudden release of water,

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:54.930
you cause like a flood effect,

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:56.440
a sudden damaging effect.

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:57.550
We've managed to wash away

00:06:57.550 --> 00:06:59.890
all the topsoil from around the tree.

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:01.500
Just in one hit.

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:03.760
Completely just gone.

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:06.040
You know, it's Texas, so the
plants need watering anyway.

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:07.500
Well to make up for this,

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:11.200
I've not run the sprinklers
for the last 18 months,

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:12.480
so the grass should enjoy that.

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:13.770
Do you mean the sprinklers you bought

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:15.330
specifically to just do a prank on me

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:16.330
and then never used?

00:07:17.810 --> 00:07:18.643
Oh .

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:22.963
That, yes, that's right.

00:07:22.963 --> 00:07:23.796
Oh yeah, okay.

00:07:23.796 --> 00:07:24.640
Well, the sprinklers were already there.

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:26.550
The controller I specifically bought.

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:27.383
Oh, okay.

00:07:27.383 --> 00:07:28.216
Yeah.

00:07:28.216 --> 00:07:29.049
I love that you're like,

00:07:29.049 --> 00:07:30.147
"Oh, I've got an automated
house with sprinklers,

00:07:30.147 --> 00:07:31.528
"never use them though."

00:07:31.528 --> 00:07:32.890
There's no point.

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:33.876
Waste of water.

00:07:33.876 --> 00:07:35.846
That's actually true.

00:07:35.846 --> 00:07:36.710
Coming from the two blokes

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:37.850
who just did that.

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:40.096
That wasn't a waste though.

00:07:40.096 --> 00:07:41.140
That was, that,

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:43.423
because we, A, watered plants.

00:07:44.950 --> 00:07:46.213
B, it was fun.

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:49.710
So, while we were just making this video,

00:07:49.710 --> 00:07:51.810
we received delivery of this,

00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:54.500
which, because this comes out in June,

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:56.340
the audience has already
seen in a lot of videos

00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:58.150
we're about to make.

00:07:58.150 --> 00:07:59.780
But for us, we just got it.

00:07:59.780 --> 00:08:00.740
So we're gonna use it.

00:08:00.740 --> 00:08:02.590
It will do twelve and a half thousand

00:08:02.590 --> 00:08:04.290
frames a second in HD.

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:05.440
So, I don't think I've ever seen

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:06.660
a giant balloon pop so slow.

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:07.870
No, I definitely haven't.

00:08:07.870 --> 00:08:10.400
Are you gonna do this one on the roof, or?

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:11.233
No.

00:08:11.233 --> 00:08:12.750
No, not gonna take this one on the roof.

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:13.583
Well, I just don't think

00:08:13.583 --> 00:08:15.030
it's gonna add a lot from the roof.

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:17.580
I wanna see it pop around the sides.

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:19.223
Three, two, one, jump!

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:24.026
I bounced off it first!

00:08:24.026 --> 00:08:27.020
It fully cushioned me
and then I landed again.

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:29.863
Oh, I got like a right
slap on my side there.

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:33.925
I'm not sure how well I got that.

00:08:33.925 --> 00:08:35.675
You fell really fast.

00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:46.410
Yeah, we've only got blue left

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:47.500
which matches the blue tarp

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:49.020
which is kind of inconvenient, actually.

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:50.740
That should suffice.

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:52.380
Looks like the balloons like an extension

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:53.213
of the tarp.

00:09:54.902 --> 00:09:55.735
The tarp.

00:09:55.735 --> 00:09:56.810
The tarp.

00:09:56.810 --> 00:09:58.193
Three, two, one, jump!

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:02.083
Jesus!

00:10:04.990 --> 00:10:07.176
You just went straight through the floor!

00:10:10.090 --> 00:10:11.290
Got absolute slapping.

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:13.543
God!

00:10:13.543 --> 00:10:14.770
The first time it did that,

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:17.420
I just like bounced slightly

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:18.500
and then landed and it broke.

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:20.675
This time I went straight through it.

00:10:20.675 --> 00:10:22.230
Just went.

00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:23.063
Yeah.

00:11:00.610 --> 00:11:01.443
That looked quite refreshing.

00:11:01.443 --> 00:11:02.276
Oh, really was.

00:11:02.276 --> 00:11:03.750
Yeah.
I'm nice a refreshed now,

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:04.740
you must be nice and hot.

00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:06.027
I am hot, it was very hot up on the roof.

00:11:06.027 --> 00:11:07.540
And I didn't break anything!

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:08.373
Very happy with that.

00:11:08.373 --> 00:11:09.920
I'm also happy I didn't
slip through the roof

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:11.260
and fall into the house.

00:11:11.260 --> 00:11:12.960
Yeah.
Although, holding a Phantom,

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:15.410
that would've been an
interesting piece of footage.

00:11:15.410 --> 00:11:16.243
You should've done this,

00:11:16.243 --> 00:11:18.187
if you landed, you'd just gone,

00:11:18.187 --> 00:11:19.640
"Push the button!"

00:11:19.640 --> 00:11:21.640
Trigger it.
Triggered it, yeah.

00:11:21.640 --> 00:11:24.850
Hopefully you enjoyed that
lovely giant balloon video.

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:27.850
Feel free to follow us on
the various social medias,

00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:29.440
it's all in the description.

00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:31.080
Instagram.
Yeah.

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:33.590
We're more Instagram boys these days.

